P1 Badge Wire the processor into a running scheduler

This processor is only defined/exported; a repo-wide search for processDueJobs finds no call from src/server.ts, any route, or a worker/cron entrypoint. In that deployment context the new scheduling paths only insert SCHEDULED rows, so enabled follow-up automation never actually sends due jobs unless some out-of-repo process is added.


In src/services/follow-up.service.ts:

> +        const monthlySends = await tx.followUpSendLog.count({
+          where: {
+            business: { businessAccountId: job.business.businessAccountId },
+            deliveryStatus: { in: [...FOLLOW_UP_MONTHLY_LIMIT_DELIVERY_STATUSES] },
+            createdAt: { gte: subscription.currentPeriodStart, lt: subscription.currentPeriodEnd },
+          },
+        });
+        if (monthlySends >= defaultMonthlyLimit(subscription.plan.code)) {
P2 Badge Reserve quota before releasing the lock

When multiple processors run and the account has one follow-up left, each worker can acquire this advisory lock, see the same monthlySends count, then release the transaction before any FollowUpSendLog is written later after WhatsApp delivery. Because no QUEUED/SENT reservation is created while the lock is held, concurrent jobs can all pass this check and exceed the monthly plan limit.


In src/services/follow-up.service.ts:

