+      where: { businessId: actor.businessId, type: input.type },
+      select: { id: true, deletedAt: true },
+    });
+    if (existingRule) {
+      throw new AppError(409, "A follow-up rule for this type already exists.", "FOLLOW_UP_RULE_ALREADY_EXISTS", {
P2 Badge Allow recreating soft-deleted rule types

After deleteRule sets deletedAt, the row still matches this lookup and the schema also has a unique key on (businessId, type), so trying to recreate that rule type always returns 409. Since getRule/updateRule exclude deleted rows, users have no restore path and a single delete permanently consumes that follow-up type for the business.
